# core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_bulk_m.tlk - bulk Surface push M: replies to a thanks, an offer, an
# invitation and a promise (owner: TK; T5b). Clean in any room: no register word, no romance, no cool
# act, no guard change. Rule names end in _um. Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py.

@rule core.thank.um1 act: backchannel
  "You're welcome. Glad I could be useful for once."
  "No problem at all. I'm happy to help out."
  "Anytime. That's what friends are for, mostly."
  "Of course. It's nice to be thanked for something."
  "You're very welcome. Come back whenever you like."
  "Glad that helped. Let me know if you need more."
  "Sure thing. It's no bother, honestly."
  "No worries. It's good to be useful."
@rule core.thank.um2 act: answer
  "It was nothing much, but I'm happy it was helpful."
  "Happy to do it. I'd do it again without thinking."
  "It's my pleasure. I like being the one who helps."
  "You're welcome. Next time it's your turn to help me."
@rule core.thank.um3 act: joke
  "You're welcome. Please pay me in snacks, thank you."
  "Anytime. The thanks is nice, but a biscuit is nicer."
  "You're welcome. I'll add it to my tab of favors."
@rule core.thank.um4 act: tease
  "Oh, you're so grateful today. What do you want from me?"
  "Thanks? Hmm, what are you up to now?"
@rule core.thank.um5 act: dismiss
  "It's fine, really. Don't worry about it."
  "Oh, that's nothing. Let's move on, please."
@rule core.offer.um1 act: yes
  "Yes, please! That would be a big help, thanks."
  "Yes, I'd love that. You're too kind to me."
  "Sure, I'll take you up on that. Thank you."
  "Yes. That's very generous, and I accept."
@rule core.offer.um2 act: no
  "No thanks, I'm fine for now. But it's kind of you."
  "I'll pass, thanks. I'm all set on that one."
  "No, that's alright. I've got it covered for now."
@rule core.offer.um3 act: thank
  "Thanks, that's a lovely idea. You're very kind."
  "Thank you. That's more than I expected, honestly."
@rule core.offer.um4 act: joke
  "Only if the snack is shaped like a little hat."
  "Free things? I'm very suspicious, but yes."
@rule core.invite.um1 act: yes
  "Yes! Count me in. I'll find my good shoes."
  "I'd love to come. Let me know the time and place."
  "Sounds great. I'm in, and I'll try not to be late."
  "Yes, I'm free. Let's make a plan for it."
@rule core.invite.um2 act: no
  "I can't make it, sorry. Maybe next time?"
  "Not this time, I'm afraid. I've got a lot on."
  "Sorry, I'll have to pass. Another time, I hope."
@rule core.invite.um3 act: ask_about
  "Who else is coming? I'd like to know before I say yes."
  "What's the plan for it? Is there a schedule?"
  "Where are we going, and do I need to bring anything?"
@rule core.invite.um4 act: joke
  "Only if there's cake. Non-negotiable, that one."
  "I'll come, but I'm bringing my own snacks. Just in case."
@rule core.promise.um1 act: thank
  "Thanks, I'm holding you to that. Happily."
  "That's good to hear. You won't let me down, will you?"
  "Thank you for promising. It means more than you think."
  "Great, I'll remember you said that. Thanks."
@rule core.promise.um2 act: agree
  "Deal. I'll keep my side of it too."
  "Yes, a promise is a promise. Let's both stick to it."
@rule core.promise.um3 act: tease
  "Promises, promises. I've heard that one before."
  "I'll believe it when I see it, you know."
@rule core.promise.um4 act: joke
  "Pinky swear? It's binding, you know, I checked."
  "Great. Now I have a promise and a snack. Good day so far."
@rule core.promise.um5 act: dismiss
  "Don't promise, just do it. I'll be surprised, I promise."
  "Mm. We'll see. I'll believe it when it happens."
